Relations: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines standard relation types for .sdd knowledge graph.

RelationTypes:
  CREATED_BY:
    Node was created by another node
  IMPLEMENTS:
    Node implements another node
  DEPENDS_ON:
    Node depends on another node
  BLOCKED_BY:
    Node is blocked by another node
  USES:
    Node uses another node
  TESTED_BY:
    Node is tested by another node
  VERIFIED_BY:
    Node is verified by another node
  SECURED_BY:
    Node is secured by another node
  DEPLOYED_BY:
    Node is deployed by another node
  RUNS_ON:
    Node runs on another node
  DOCUMENTED_BY:
    Node is documented by another node
  CAUSED_BY:
    Node was caused by another node
  AFFECTS:
    Node affects another node
  OWNS:
    Node owns another node
  RELATED_TO:
    Node is related to another node
  REPLACES:
    Node replaces another node
  SUPERSEDES:
    Node supersedes another node
  CONFLICTS_WITH:
    Node conflicts with another node

RelationRules:
  [RL1]  Relations are directional.
  [RL2]  Relations use standard types.
  [RL3]  Multiple relations between nodes are allowed.
  [RL4]  Relations enable forward and reverse traversal.

State: +
  
